  "raw": {
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/South-Street-Campus/Aboriginal-and-Torres-Strait-Islander-Talent-Register_JR102224": {
      "title": "Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Talent Register",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-15\n\nAbout Us Situated on Whadjuk and Binjareb Noongar lands, Murdoch University was founded over 40 years ago on principles of social inclusion, equity and free-thinking. Today, we remain a university for all, irrespective of social, cultural, or economic backgrounds. We invite you to help us achieve our goals – and yours – by registering your interest in career opportunities through our talent register. Join the team! Are you of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage? Are you looking to advance your career in an inclusive and supportive atmosphere? We invite you to express your interest in joining our team. Current Murdoch students are especially encouraged to register.   Simply click ‘Apply’ to begin the process and submit your up-to-date resume. Next Steps! By registering, you will become part of our candidate pool and will be considered for current job openings. We are committed to increasing the representation of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander employees, your skills and experience may even lead to the creation of new positions. A member of our People and Culture team may contact you to discuss the types of opportunities you are interested in. Registration on the talent register does not guarantee an employment offer, however it can make it easier for you to be considered for future positions. Prior to any placements, regular selection and screening processes will apply in line with our Recruitment Policy. Questions? We’re here to help! If you have any queries please reach out to our Senior Advisor First Nations - Allana Sheppard at Allana.Sheppard@murdoch.edu.au Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Agricultural-Science-Teaching-and-Learning-Talent-Register_JR105577": {
      "title": "Agricultural Science Teaching and Learning Talent Register",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-13\n\nAbout The Team The School of Agricultural Science at Murdoch University is shaping the future of agriculture through excellence in teaching, research and industry engagement. Our teaching and learning activities prepare graduates to address challenges in food and fibre production, animal health and biosecurity. We deliver undergraduate and postgraduate degrees, together with research training programs. Our coursework offerings include majors in: Animal Science Animal Health Crop and Pasture Science Biosecurity Food Security The team also delivers minors in Equine Science and Agribusiness. Our teaching and learning programs combine strong foundational knowledge with hands-on learning through laboratories, fieldwork and industry placements, equipping students with the skills and networks needed for careers in modern agriculture, animal health and biosecurity. About the opportunity We invite expressions of interest from candidates with relevant academic and/or industry experience to join our teaching talent register for casual and fixed-term opportunities within the School of Agricultural Science. Lectures Workshops, laboratory classes and field-based teaching activities Tutorials Marking Animal handling demonstration involving horses, cattle, sheep and pigs We welcome applications from both experienced educators and industry professionals who can bring contemporary knowledge and real-world perspectives to student learning. Please register for the talent pool online via the Apply Now button. The following documents should be submitted to support your application: A cover letter that includes: an outline of your areas of expertise and relevant experience subject areas and teaching activities of interest availability for face-to-face teaching at the Murdoch University South Street Campus and/or online delivery Your most recent resume (CV) detailing academic qualifications, teaching experience and relevant professional industry experience This Talent Register will remain active until 31st August 2027 Candidates whose skills and experience align with emerging teaching needs may be considered for casual or fixed-term teaching opportunities as they arise. Please note: successful candidates may be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Visa sponsorship is not available for positions that will be filled from this talent register. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity please reach out to agscience@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105577 as the reference. Applications for this talent register close on 31 August 2027 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Peel-WA/Lecturer-of-Nursing_JR105180": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer or Lecturer in Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The School of Nursing is a highly engaged, supportive and innovative academic team within the College of Health and Education. Our collegial culture is underpinned by a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research and professional practice, with many team members recognised through national, state, university and industry awards. Working closely with extensive clinical partners and active national and international research collaborators, the Nursing team provides high-quality, student-focused learning experiences across undergraduate, postgraduate and research programs. Your New Role!   We are seeking two Associate Lecturers or Lecturers in Nursing to join our team. These positions are primarily based at our South Street campus in Murdoch; however, the successful applicants will also be required to teach at our Mandurah campus, with time allocated across both locations in line with teaching and operational requirements. As an Associate Lecturer , you will contribute to teaching, research and service within the School of Nursing while developing your academic profile under the guidance of senior academics. Key responsibilities: Deliver high-quality teaching across Nursing programs and campuses as required. Contribute to nursing research and scholarly outputs. Engage with the School, College, University and nursing profession. Work collaboratively across diverse healthcare and educational settings. As a Lecturer , you will undertake independent teaching, research and scholarly activity, making a significant contribution through your professional expertise and academic leadership. Key responsibilities: Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate Nursing programs. Conduct and lead nursing research, producing high-quality scholarly outputs. Engage with the School, College, University and nursing profession. Contribute to the coordination and leadership of academic activities. Work collaboratively across diverse healthcare and educational settings. Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement below for each role. Associate Lecturer Lecturer What We Offer You! This Continuous | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of: Associate Lecturer $81,513 – $109,925 (pro rata) Lecturer $115,512 – $136,831 (pro rata) Plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Associate Lecturer A degree in Nursing and a relevant postgraduate qualification at AQF Level 8 or above (or equivalent professional experience recognised by the University). Progress towards a higher degree, such as a PhD, is desirable. Current unrestricted AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. Ability to deliver evidence-based teaching using contemporary nursing education practices. Experience in nursing education with positive student outcomes. Experience contributing to curriculum development and quality teaching initiatives. Lecturer A PhD in Nursing or a related discipline (or equivalent professional experience). Current unrestricted AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. Experience delivering high-quality teaching and applying contemporary nursing education practices. Experience in nursing education with positive student outcomes. Ability to contribute to curriculum development, teaching excellence and educational innovation. Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia.  Relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Frank Donnelly, Dean of Nursing, frank.donnelly@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105180 as the reference. Applications Close on 18 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Lecturer-in-Engineering_JR105172": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Engineering is an academic discipline within the School of Engineering and Energy. The Engineering team teach key and emerging areas of Engineering at the undergraduate and postgraduate levels. We specialize in Environmental Engineering, Electrical and Renewable Energy Engineering and industrial Control & Automation Engineering. Industrial Control & Automation Engineering at Murdoch highlights a strong practical, industry-relevant learning approach, built around authentic, workshop-based activities that develop hands-on technical and professional skills. The area includes a focus on control theory and control systems, including PLC and SCADA systems, aligned with real-world design, commissioning, and implementation needs in local industry sectors. More broadly, Murdoch Engineering is nationally recognised and has a strong track record of student outcomes, including high rankings in QILT for overall quality of educational experience in Engineering. Engineering is taught at the Murdoch campus and offshore. Your New Role!   We are seeking a Lecturer (Level B) or Senior Lecturer (Level C) to join our Industrial Control and Automation Engineering discipline within the School of Engineering and Energy. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to a nationally recognised Engineering program through high-quality teaching, impactful research and industry engagement. You will teach across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, contribute to curriculum innovation and help prepare graduates for careers in rapidly evolving engineering industries. The successful candidate will have expertise in Industrial Control & Automation Engineering or a related field, with experience in areas such as control systems, industrial automation, instrumentation, PLCs, SCADA systems, robotics, mechatronics or intelligent automation. Based at our South Street campus, this position also includes teaching at one of Murdoch University's partner institutions in China. The successful candidate will be willing and able to undertake two international teaching visits each year, typically totalling four to six months annually. Your Key responsibilities will include – Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate Engineering programs. Contribute to curriculum development and continuous improvement of courses and units. Conduct impactful research and contribute to scholarly publications. Engage with industry and professional stakeholders to enhance teaching and research outcomes. Supervise honours and postgraduate students, as appropriate to level. Contribute to School, College and University service activities. Teach at Murdoch University's partner institution in China. Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details.   Level B Level C   What We Offer You! This Continuous, Full Time attracts a remuneration of:   Lecturer Level B : $115,512 - $136,831 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.   Senior Lecturer Level C $141,088 - $162,403 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: A PhD in Industrial Control & Automation Engineering or a closely related discipline. Expertise in one or more areas including industrial automation, control systems, PLCs, SCADA systems, instrumentation, robotics, mechatronics or intelligent automation. Demonstrated teaching experience at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to work collaboratively. Commitment to high-quality teaching, research and student outcomes. Ability and willingness to undertake international teaching visits in China. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to David Parlevliet , Dean of Engineering and Energy, and quote JR105172 as the reference. Applications Close on 26th October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Centre-Director--Australian-National-Phenome-Centre--ANPC-_JR105851": {
      "title": "Centre Director, Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC) is a national Core Facility for high-resolution metabolic phenotyping and translational bioscience. Based within the Harry Perkins Institute of Medical Research in Perth’s Murdoch Health Precinct, the Centre integrates advanced Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR), mass spectrometry, automation and bioinformatics platforms to support industrial-scale biological analysis and population-scale phenotyping at the interface of research, healthcare and industry. The ANPC is a key platform within Murdoch University’s Health Futures Institute. The Centre supports research across a broad range of disciplines, including precision medicine and human health, population health and epidemiology, chronic disease prevention, nutrition and metabolic health, agriculture and food systems, environmental science, and systems biology research. For more information about the Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC) please refer to the ANPC brochure . Your New Role!   Reporting to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research and Innovation, the Centre Director provides strategic, scientific and operational leadership for the Australian National Phenome Centre (ANPC). The role is responsible for setting the Centre’s vision and direction, maximising the impact of its infrastructure, and positioning the Centre as globally recognised leader in precision health, translational bioscience and population-scale discovery. You will lead a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technical specialists, drive intentionally competitive research programs, secure major research investment, and support the translation of research outcomes into clinical, public health, commercial and societal impact. Murdoch University welcomes expressions of interest from Associate Professors, recently appointment Professors and equivalent research leaders seeking to broaden their impact through the leadership of a nationally significant research capability. Your key responsibilities will include – Provide strategic, scientific and operational leadership for ANPC, setting the Centre’s vision and direction and maximising the impact of its research infrastructure Drive internationally competitive research programs and secure major research investment to advance prevision health, phenomics and translational research Build strategic partnership across academia, healthcare, government, and industry to support research translation and impact Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement and the ANPC Brochure for further details.   What We Offer You! This, Fixed Term (5 Years) | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts the following remuneration: $217,824.00 (pro rata) at the Academic Level E plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, potential market loading will be considered for the right candidate undefined $169,509.00 to 186,557.00 (pro rata) at the Academic Level D plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, potential market loading will be considered for the right candidate    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: ·         Flexible work arrangements ·         Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role ·         Indigenous Language Allowance ·         Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit ·         Employee Assistance Program ·         On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV)   What you’ll bring to the role: A doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) in a relevant discipline such as biomedical science, health and medical research, metabolomics, systems biology, population health, bioinformatics, precision health or a closely related field. Internationally recognised expertise in precision health, metabolomics, phenomics, systems biology or a related biomedical discipline Demonstrated success in leading large-scale translational, clinical, cohort, epidemiology or multidisciplinary research programs A strong track record in securing competitive research funding and developing internationally competitive research programs Proven ability to translate research outcomes into clinical, public health, policy, industry, innovation or commercial applications with evidence of national and/or international research impact Ability to undertake domestic and international travel and work across Murdoch University campuses, the Australia National Phenome Centre (ANPC), partner organisations and clinical and research precincts as required Ability to work within laboratory, clinical, cohort and research environments to support research programs and strategic initiative Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure.   Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Peter Eastwood, Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research and Innovation, Peter.Eastwood@murdoch.edu.au , and quote JR105851 as the reference.   Applications Close on 05 November 2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Research-Fellow-or-Principal-Research-Fellow_JR105738": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow or Principal Research Fellow",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Food Futures Institute is one of Murdoch University’s research institutes, focused on developing innovating solutions for sustainable food, forestry, and fibre production. This position is based within the Centre for Crop and Food Innovation (CCFI) and the State Agricultural Biotechnology Centre (SABC). CCFI conducts research in broadacre and horticultural crops, bringing together academic and research staff who work with industry partners to improve crop yield, quality and resilience. The Centre also supports more than 50 Higher Degree by Research students and is ideally place to capitalise on new technologies and investments in crop agriculture. SABC is Western Australia’s collaborative university-based centre for agricultural and veterinary biotechnology, providing access to specialised technologies, equipment and research facilities that support collaboration across agricultural, environmental and conversation, molecular, biomedical and veterinary sciences.   Your New Role!   We are seeking to appoint either a Senior Research Fellow (Level C) or a Principal Research Fellow (Level D) in Murdoch University, South Street Campus. As a Senior Research Fellow (Level C) , you are expected to lead and coordinate innovative genomics and pre- breeding research to advance genetic gain in pulse crops. The role involves delivering multidisciplinary research programs, including field trials, genotyping and sequencing, genomic and bioinformatics analyses, and AI-enabled breeding approaches. You will contribute to genomic resource development, public research outcomes, secure competitive funding, supervise HDR students and research staff, and collaborate with national and international research partners. Working closely with the Director of CCFI/SABC, you will provide scientific leadership in the successful delivery of GRDC-funded project, Achieving Improved Genetic Gain for Yield in Chickpea, Faba Bean and Lentil Using Genetic Diversity, while contributing to Murdoch University’s strategic research priorities in Food and Agriculture. As a Principal Research Fellow (Level D), you will provide strategic leadership in genomics, functional genomics, pre- breeding and AI-enabled crop improvement across wheat, pulse and horticultural crop research programs. This role involves developing and leading internationally recognised research programs integrating genomics, phenomics, bioinformatics and artificial intelligence, establishing multi-disciplinary research initiatives, fostering strategic partnerships, securing major research funding, supervising and mentoring researchers, and driving the strategic growth and international reputation of CCFI, SABC and Murdoch University. Your key responsibilities will include – Senior Research Fellow (Level C) Provide strategic leadership in developing and delivering innovative research programs aligned with CCFI priorities, enhancing national and international research impact Lead internationally competitive research in genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, AI-enabled crop improvement, and related disciplines Build and maintain strategic collaborations with universities, government, industry, and international partners to advance multidisciplinary and translational research outcomes Secure competitive research funding, leading major grant applications, and oversee high-quality research programs including glasshouse, controlled-environment, and field-based experiments Apply advanced genomics, sequencing bioinformatics, molecular genetics, and AI methodologies to deliver impactful crop improvement and agricultural biotechnology outcomes, translating research into practical applications Publish high-quality scholarly outputs, supervise and mentor HDR students and research staff, contribute to teaching and postgraduate education, and provide leadership in governance, strategic planning, and professional service activities Principal Research Fellow (Level D) Drive and shape internationally recognised research programs in plant genomics, molecular breeding, artificial intelligence, and crop improvement across diverse agricultural systems Lead multidisciplinary research teams and deliver innovative solutions to challenges in crop improvement, sustainable agriculture, and food security, aligned with the University and national research priorities Design and oversee complex laboratory, glasshouse, controlled-environment and field-related research programs, applying advanced genomics, sequencing, bioinformatics, quantitative genetics, and AI enabled approaches Secure major national and international research funding, develop industry partnership and build strategic collaborations with universities, government agencies, industry, CGIAR centres, and global research organisations Translate research discoveries into practical breeding and agricultural applications, promoting industry adoption, commercialisation, and stakeholder engagement Produce high-impact research outputs, contribute to the strategic growth and reputation of CCFI and SABC, and provide academic leadership, mentorship, governance, and professional service within the University and broader research community   Please refer to the Position Descriptions for further details. ·       Senior Research Fellow (Level C) ·       Principal Research Fellow (Level D)   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (3 years) |Full Time (37.5 hours per week) position attracts a remuneration of the following Level C $141,088- $162,403 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions Level D $169,509 - $186,557 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions   You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   ·       Flexible work arrangements ·       Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role ·       Indigenous Language Allowance ·       Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit ·       Employee Assistance Program ·       On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - ·       A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: Senior Research Fellow (Level C) PhD in Agricultural Biotechnology, Genetics, Plant Breeding or any other relevant subject with at least five years’ research experience in crop genomics and pre-breeding, and an established national and emerging international research reputation Demonstrated ability to develop, lead and manage independent research programs in genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, crop improvement or related fields, supported by a strong publication record Proven success in securing research outcomes through multidisciplinary projects, collaboration with industry, government and international partners, and translating research into impact Demonstrated experience supervising and mentoring HDR students, postdoctoral researchers and research staff, with strong leadership, organisational and project management skills Excellent communication skills, including scientific publications, grant writing and presentations, together with a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and a safe, respectful workplace Principal Research Fellow (Level D) PhD in Plant Science, Plant Genetics, Plant Breeding, Genomics, Agricultural Biotechnology, or a related discipline, with an internationally recognised reputation and outstanding research impact in plant genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, quantitative genetics or related fields Demonstrated success leading internationally competitive research programs, securing major national and international research funding, and delivering significant scientific, industry and societal outcomes Expertise in plant genomics, functional genomics, molecular breeding, quantitative genetics, high-throughput sequencing technologies, bioinformatics, artificial intelligence, and digital technologies of crop improvement Proven ability to lead multidisciplinary and multi-institutional research teams, establish strategic collaborations, and build impactful partnership across universities, industry, government and international organisations Demonstrated academic leadership through supervision and mentoring of researchers and HDR students, strategic contributions to research capacity building and governance, and a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and research integrity   Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Rajeev Varshney, Director of the State Agricultural Biotechnology Centre and Director of the Centre for Crop and Food, rajeev.varshney@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105738 as the reference.   Applications Close on 01/11/2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinary-Nurse--Medicine-_JR105876": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse (Medicine)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team   The Small Animal Internal Medicine, Oncology, and Cardiology service at The Animal Hospital delivers comprehensive care for a wide range of complex medical conditions affecting dogs and cats. Employing advanced diagnostic modalities such as video endoscopy, ultrasonography, digital radiography, CT, MRI, electrocardiography, blood pressure monitoring, and supported by an on-site laboratory, we provide prompt and accurate diagnostics. Our facility features a fully equipped ICU for 24-hour critical care as well as a dedicated Oncology suite for chemotherapy administration. Collaborating with dermatology, surgery, critical care, pathology, imaging, and anaesthesia teams, we adopt a multidisciplinary approach for holistic and patient-centred care. Team members will regularly communicate with referring veterinarians, so the best and most convenient patient care is offered to our clients for their pets. You would be joining a team of 7 veterinary nurses with the service open to clientele 08:00 -18:00 Weekdays. Your New Role!   The key purpose of this role is to provide high-quality veterinary nursing care to animals in The Animal Hospital At Murdoch University. Your Key responsibilities will include – Provide all aspects of veterinary nursing care as per the Certificate IV of Veterinary Nursing and the Prescribed Duties of Veterinary Nurses within the Vet Surgeons Act of WA. Comply with University and TAHMU policies, procedures and protocols. Comply with The Veterinary Surgeons’ Act of WA and other veterinary industry related Acts and Regulations. Liaise with clinical areas within the hospital to coordinate daily availability of equipment and technical support. Assist clinicians with examinations, workups, procedures, treatments and surgeries. Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Month) | Part time or Full Time (up to 37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $74,809K – $79,802K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, with the option to sacrifice 5% of your superannuation into your salary.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)   What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or equivalent, or completion of a relevant Veterinary Nursing Diploma level qualification registrable in Western Australia. Demonstrated confidence and skill when handling and restraining small animals. Excellent knowledge of diagnostic and medical equipment as well as sterilising and aseptic techniques. Excellent organisational, time and workload management skills, including the ability to prioritise workload to meet strict deadlines. Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills, and the demonstrated ability to interact constructively and collaboratively with staff at all levels of the organisation. Demonstrated ability to use initiative, assume responsibility for tasks and projects and to resolve problems. Proven ability to work independently as well as fitting seamlessly into a team environment. A strong interest in developing nursing skills within a specialised area   Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Ailsa Brown, Medicine Coordinator, A.Brown@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105876 as the reference.   Applications Close on 23rd October 2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Research-Fellow_JR105868": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate/Research Fellow - Feral Cat Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The research program is led by the Harry Butler Institute (HBI). HBI is one of the three Murdoch University Institutes that bring together leading researchers from across the University to deliver world class interdisciplinary research that benefits the environment. HBI researchers work directly with the government, industry, and the community towards protecting the environment with relevant, applied research outcomes. This project reflects a collaboration between Murdoch University and industry partners. It is based within the Centre for Terrestrial Ecosystem Science and Sustainability (TESS). TESS brings together academic staff and research students working with community and industry partners to advance biodiversity conservation through high-quality scientific research. Your New Role!   Murdoch University is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate (Level A) or a Research Fellow (Level B) to support a research project focused on feral cat management and biodiversity conservation in the Northern Jarrah Forest. Working with Murdoch researchers and external stakeholders, you will contribute to (and at Level B, help lead) field-based research, including survey and monitoring activities, population management approaches, and data analysis to inform conservation outcomes. Your key responsibilities will include – Postdoctoral Research Associate (Level A) Support field-based research, including vertebrate fauna surveys and application of animal ethics and permit requirements Contribute to data analysis and scholarly outputs, including reports, publications and presentations Collaborate within a multidisciplinary team and contribute to research, supervision and broader academic activities Research Fellow (Level B) Lead and contribute to experimental design, field-based research, and monitoring of vertebrate fauna, including animal ethics and permit requirements Analyse research data and produce high-quality outputs, including publications, reports, presentations, and funding applications Support project leadership, collaboration, and supervision of students and research staff   Please refer to the Position Descriptions for further details: Postdoctoral Research Associate (Level A) Position Description Research Fellow (Level B) Position Description   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (4 Years) | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts the following remuneration: Postdoctoral Research Associate - $81,513 - $109,925 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions Research Fellow - $115,512 - $136,831 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: Postdoctoral Research Associate (Level A) PhD (or near completion) in Ecology, Wildlife Biology, Conservation Biology, or a related field Experience in fieldwork and project coordination Strong statistical skills, including experience analysing large data sets (e.g. camera-trap data) Ability to undertake independent research with limited supervision Excellent communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to engage a range of stakeholders Research Fellow (Level B) PhD in Ecology, Wildlife Biology, Conservation Biology, or a related field Proven experience in project coordination, fieldwork, and stakeholder engagement Strong statistical and analytical skills, with experience managing large datasets Demonstrated research track record, including publications and success in research funding applications Excellent communication, collaboration, and supervision skills within multidisciplinary environments Please note, the successful candidate will require a willingness and ability to travel within the state on a regular basis, and work in remote field sites and outside of normal office hours when required.   Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia.   Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Professor Trish Fleming, t.fleming@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR10868 as the reference   Applications Close on 01/11/2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Sustainable-Farm-Project-Officer_JR105740": {
      "title": "Sustainable Farm Project Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nPart time\n\nAbout The Team Our Sustainability team is passionate, collaborative and dedicated to driving sustainability initiatives across Murdoch University's campuses and farms. Working across Sustainability Ethos, Climate Action and Nature Positive priorities, the team delivers projects that create meaningful environmental outcomes. In this role, you'll contribute to Murdoch University's Nature Positive aspirations by supporting biodiversity, habitat restoration and sustainable land management initiatives across the University's unique farm and conservation landscapes.   Your New Role!   As the Sustainable Farm Project Officer, you will play a key role in delivering innovative farm regeneration and environmental restoration projects across Murdoch University's South Street campus. Working as part of the Office of the PVC Sustainability, you will help enhance biodiversity, expand wildlife corridors, restore wetlands and native habitats and support nature positive outcomes across the University's farms and surrounding conservation areas.   In this newly created role, you'll work closely with sustainability specialists, farm teams, researchers and academic staff to implement on-ground projects, coordinate contractors, monitor project outcomes, and contribute to major sustainability initiatives supported by significant external funding. Your work will directly support Murdoch University's environmental goals and long-term sustainability strategy.   Key Responsibilities Deliver sustainable farming, environmental restoration, and biodiversity projects in collaboration with key stakeholders. Coordinate contractors and service providers undertaking restoration works, including weed management, fencing, revegetation, and site maintenance. Support habitat restoration across farms, wetlands, woodlands, and conservation areas. Monitor project outcomes, maintain project records, and assist with reporting against project objectives, budgets, and timelines. Source and apply best-practice advice on ecological restoration, weed management, and native vegetation establishment.     Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (2 Years) | Part time (15 hours per week) attracts a starting salary of $93k (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.  The position is also eligible for salary step progression within the classification level in accordance with Murdoch University's Enterprise Agreement.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: A Bachelor’s degree or Diploma in Sustainable Agriculture, Soil Science, Environmental Management, or a related field. Experience delivering environmental restoration projects, particularly in sensitive ecological environments. Demonstrated experience managing environmental management contractors and services. Knowledge of environmental weed control and ecological restoration practices. A current Class C Driver’s Licence. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Leah Knapp, Manager Sustainability, l.knapp@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105740 as the reference.  Applications Close on 21 October 2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Veterinary-Nurse--Surgery--1_JR105618": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse (Surgery)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The small animal surgery referral service offers specialty services in both soft tissue and oncologic surgery, and orthopaedic and neurosurgery. Our full range of facilities and state of the art surgical equipment, coupled with integrated support from specialist level care in anaesthesia, 24h intensive care, internal medicine, advanced diagnostic imaging and excellent nursing standards enable us to manage the most complex surgical challenges and ensure that our patients receive a very high standard of care across all aspects of surgical management. You would be joining a team of 7 veterinary nurses; the service is open to clientele 08:00 -18:00 Weekdays. Your New Role!   The key purpose of this role is to provide high quality veterinary nursing care to animals in The Animal Hospital At Murdoch University. Your Key responsibilities will include – Provide all aspects of veterinary nursing care as per the Certificate IV of Veterinary Nursing and the Prescribed Duties of Veterinary Nurses within the Vet Surgeons Act of WA. Comply with University and TAHMU policies, procedures and protocols. Comply with The Veterinary Surgeons’ Act of WA and other veterinary industry related Acts and Regulations. Liaise with clinical areas within the hospital to coordinate daily availability of equipment and technical support. Assist clinicians with examinations, workups, procedures, treatments and surgeries. Please refer to the Position Description for further details. What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (12 Month) | Part time or Full Time (up to 37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $74,809K – $79,802K (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions, with the option to sacrifice 5% of your superannuation into your salary.    You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030. As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page ! Join us! Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV) What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or equivalent, or completion of a relevant Veterinary Nursing Diploma level qualification registrable in Western Australia. Demonstrated confidence and skill when handling and restraining small animals. Excellent knowledge of diagnostic and surgical equipment as well as sterilising and aseptic techniques. Demonstrated experience and exposure to various surgical procedures and patient care in a general practice setting. Excellent organisational, time and workload management skills, including the ability to prioritise workload to meet strict deadlines. Highly effective communication, customer service and interpersonal skills, and the demonstrated ability to interact constructively and collaboratively with staff at all levels of the organisation. Demonstrated ability to use initiative, assume responsibility for tasks and projects and to resolve problems. Proven ability to work independently as well as fitting seamlessly into a team environment. A strong interest in developing skills within a specialised area. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Sam Watkins , Surgery Coordinator, sam.watkins@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105618 as the reference. Applications Close on 23rd October 2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
