    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Senior-Lecturer_JR105891": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer University Preparation Pathways",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nAbout The Team The University Preparation Pathways (UPP) team sits within the Office of the DVC (Education) and provides integrated leadership and support across access, teaching and learning initiatives at Murdoch University. The team play a critical role in supporting students as they transition into higher education, deliver engaging learning experience that build confidence, capability and academic success. The team is committed to excellence in teaching and learning, innovation in pedagogy, and creating accessible pathways that enable a diverse range of students to achieve their higher education aspirations.   Your New Role!   As a Senior Lecturer, you will play a leading role in delivering high-quality teaching, driving impactful research and contributing to the ongoing development of Enabling education at Murdoch University. You will provide academic leadership across STEM-related disciplines, fostering student engagement and success through innovative curriculum design, contemporary teaching practice and scholarly activity. Your key responsibilities will include – Lead the delivery of innovative teaching and learning experiences across undergraduate and pathway programs, including face-to-face, online and blended learning environments. Design, review and enhance curriculum, learning resources and assessment practices that support student success and meet regulatory and academic quality standards. Provide academic leadership in STEM and Enabling education, contributing to the development of contemporary teaching approaches and learning innovations. Undertake and lead research activities that contribute to disciplinary knowledge, educational practice and institutional priorities. Build collaborative relationships with academic colleagues, industry and external stakeholders that enhance educational and research outcomes. Attract research funding, supervise higher degree research students and contribute to a culture of research excellence. Lead laboratory and fieldwork activities supporting student learning across multiple delivery modes and campus locations. Contribute to University governance, committees, service activities and broader academic leadership initiatives.   Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Continuous | Part Time (30 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $141,088 – $162,403 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: A PhD in a relevant STEM, Life Sciences or related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in STEM and/or Life Sciences teaching and scholarship, with the ability to engage and support a diverse student cohort. Evidence of high-quality teaching practice and curriculum development across higher education settings. A strong track record of research and scholarly contribution with an emerging or established national reputation. Experience applying quantitative research methodologies and laboratory-based skills. Demonstrated success in leading and collaborating within multidisciplinary academic environments. Experience supervising students and fostering a culture of learning, research and academic excellence. Strong interpersonal, communication and stakeholder engagement skills. A commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and student success.   Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process. Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Dr. Noraisha Oyama, Head of University Preparation Pathways n.oyama@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105891 as the reference.   Applications Close on 29/10/2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer-in-Food-Science_JR105843": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Food Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nMurdoch, WA About The Team Join a collaborative and research-active School driving innovation across health, food science, nutrition and forensic sciences. With a strong focus on student success, industry engagement and impactful research, the team delivers high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate programs that prepare graduates to make a difference in the real world.   Your New Role!   As a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Food Science and Nutrition, you will contribute to excellence in teaching, research and industry engagement. You will develop and deliver innovative learning experiences across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, supervise research students, grow a research profile in your area of expertise, build meaningful industry partnerships, and support the ongoing enhancement of our Food Science and Nutrition courses. Your Key responsibilities will include – Development, delivery, assessment, review, and coordination of units in the Bachelor of Food Science and Nutrition and the Master of Food Science. Developing and growing a research program integrating postgraduate training and supervision in food science, nutrition, food chemistry, and/or food safety, and/or related fields, that complement the teaching and research activities of the School and University. Developing strong industry linkages to enhance teaching experiences for students and/or grow research partnerships and collaborations. Contributing to the activities required by the course, School, and University to ensure ongoing review and improvements to the Bachelor of Food Science and Nutrition and the Master of Food Science. Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details. Level B Level C   What We Offer You! This Continuous, Full Time attracts a remuneration of:   Lecture Level B: $115,512 - $136,831 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.    Senior Lecture Level C: $141,088 - $162,403 plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.     You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including: Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria and qualification requirement(s) (Please refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement) Your most recent resume (CV)    What you’ll bring to the role: A tertiary qualification of at least four years in the relevant field, or equivalent professional experience recognised by the University. A relevant doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) in the discipline, or equivalent professional experience as recognised by the University. Maintain your professional registration or accreditation, where relevant to your discipline or profession. Professional experience in one or more areas of food science, nutrition, food production, food chemistry, and/or food safety. Eligibility to be a member of a professional body, such as the Australian Institute of Food Science and Technology (AIFST), or Nutrition Society of Australia (NSA), or related organisation. Applicants should refer to the Position Description and Duty Statement for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Visa sponsorship and relocation may be available for the right candidate. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Murray Adams, Head of School of Medical, Molecular and Forensic Sciences and quote JR105843 as the reference.   Applications Close on 12th November 2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.   Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Research-Project-Officer--YMK-_JR105929": {
      "title": "Research Project Officer (YMK)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nMurdoch University is committed to improving employment opportunities and outcomes for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. As a measure to achieve equity and support, Section 51 of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) will apply to this position.   The Ngangk Yira Institute for Change is one of the four key Murdoch University institutes that deliver world class multidisciplinary and interdisciplinary translational research that benefits the Aboriginal community, government, and industry. Ngangk Yira is founded on principles of meaningful community engagement, professional collaborations, and Aboriginal-led research. These, together with engagement of Aboriginal Elders, Aboriginal communities, and the preservation and promotion of cultural wisdom and data sovereignty, ensures Ngangk Yira is championing meaningful, co-designed research for the health and wellbeing and social equity and change for Aboriginal people, families, and communities. The team at Yorga Maaman Koolanga Research and Advocacy Centre (within Ngangk Yira) focus on supporting parents and children from pregnancy through the early years, building strong foundations for healthy, resilient families and communities. Our work brings together researchers, clinicians, Elders, community members, and policymakers to create evidence that strengthens and supports Aboriginal families every step of the way To learn more about our Centre's research groups visit: https://www.murdoch.edu.au/research/nyi/research/yorga-mamman-and-koolanga-research-advocacy-centre   Your New Role!   The Research Project Officer will support the implementation of the externally funded research program focused on improving practice and care coordination when child protection intervenes with pregnant mothers and newborns. The role will involve supporting administrative and operational elements of the research in addition to Aboriginal-led components of the project.   Ideally an Aboriginal appointment, the role is highly suited to someone with healthcare and/or research experience, and a cultural understanding of birthing for Aboriginal women and families.   Your key responsibilities will include – Providing research and project support to the Research Program and working collaboratively as part of the wider Yorga Maaman Koolanga Team. Working effectively in diverse settings engaging with internal and external stakeholders including Aboriginal organisations, health services, community members and government agencies. Assist with recruitment of participants and act as a point of contact for arranging interviews in culturally safe environments. Coordinate and facilitate focus groups, workshops, and co-design activities with lived experience consultants and community members. Maintain accurate records and databases for ethics and funding reporting and assist with the preparation of reports and applications. Develop and distribute project materials, including posters, information sheets and consent forms. Create project communications, including e-newsletters, website updates and stakeholder materials. Support cultural governance and engagement with Ngangk Yira Elders Group and Maaman Group.   Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Fixed Term (ending 30/06/2029) | Part Time (30 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $82,210 – $91,567 (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: Relevant undergraduate qualification or progress towards an undergraduate qualification and/or an equivalent combination of relevant work experience in a related area. Previous experience in a similar role, demonstrating the ability to work in an inclusive team with a diversity of cultures, ideally in an education, welfare or health sector. Excellent professional communication, teamwork and interpersonal skills with a diversity of levels of staff within a university including senior/elder cultural stakeholders. Superior time management and workload management skills.; with the ability to prioritise tasks, problem solve, use initiative and work with attention to detail. High level of computer literacy, including the ability to confidently navigate a variety of web based and desktop applications, including MS Office. Strong commitment to the principles of self-determination data sovereignty and improving social equity for diverse and marginalised cultures. Current ‘C’ Class License. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure. Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Prof. Rhonda Marriott, Pro Vice Chancellor Ngangk Yira Institute for Change at r.marriott@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105929 as the reference. Applications Close on 08/11/2026 (11:59pm AWST) The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Casual-Academic-Opportunities-in-Criminology_JR105930": {
      "title": "Casual Academic Opportunities in Criminology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\n\nSchool of Law and Criminology | Murdoch University Expressions of Interest: Summer Term and Semester 1 Murdoch University's School of Law and Criminology is seeking expressions of interest from both new and experienced casual academics interested in contributing to the delivery of our Criminology programs during the upcoming Summer Term and Semester 1 teaching periods. We are particularly interested in hearing from individuals who are passionate about student learning and capable of teaching into undergraduate and postgraduate units across a range of criminology and criminal justice disciplines. About the Role Casual academic staff play an important role in supporting the delivery of high-quality learning experiences for our students. Opportunities may arise for duties such as: Delivering lectures, tutorials and workshops Online teaching and student engagement Marking and assessment moderation Student consultation and academic support Other teaching-related activities associated with unit delivery Teaching may be offered across a variety of modes, including: Face-to-face teaching at our Perth campus Fully online or blended delivery Offshore teaching support for programs delivered through our Singapore and Dubai partnerships Appointments may range from occasional engagements in a specialist area through to more frequent, casual teaching commitments across a semester. Areas of Expertise We welcome expressions of interest from applicants with expertise in one or more areas including contemporary criminological theory, policing, corrections, crime science, white collar and corporate crime, cybercrime, and research methods.  Applicants with expertise in criminology, sociology, psychology, legal studies, criminal law, politics and public policy, forensic or other related disciplines are encouraged to apply. About Criminology at Murdoch Criminology at Murdoch University examines the causes, consequences and prevention of crime, drawing on interdisciplinary perspectives from the social sciences, law and psychology. Students explore contemporary challenges in criminal justice and develop an understanding of how societies respond to crime, victimisation and social harm. Our programs encourage students to critically analyse crime and justice issues, challenge common assumptions, and investigate evidence-based approaches to crime reduction and prevention. Areas of study include policing, criminal behaviour, crime science, corporate crime, cybercrime, international crime, and criminological research. Students also have opportunities to engage in work-integrated learning and applied experiences that connect academic study with professional practice. About the School of Law and Criminology The School of Law and Criminology is a nationally and internationally recognised centre for teaching, research and professional engagement in law, criminology and justice. As part of the College of Law, Arts and Social Sciences, the School is distinguished by its interdisciplinary approach to questions of justice, governance, social change and community wellbeing. Our academics are engaged in research and teaching across areas including social justice, human rights, policing, crime, legal practice and public policy. The School maintains strong connections with industry, government, justice agencies and community organisations, enabling our students to connect their learning with contemporary professional practice. We are committed to providing an intellectually rigorous, inclusive and student-centred learning environment that prepares graduates to contribute positively to society. Qualifications and Experience Applicants should normally possess: At least an Honours degree in Criminology or a closely related discipline; and Relevant professional, industry or teaching experience. Preference will be given to applicants who hold: A Master's degree or Doctoral qualification in a relevant field; Previous tertiary teaching experience; and/or Current or recent professional experience within criminology, criminal justice, policing, corrections, government, policy or related sectors. How to Express Interest To express interest, please submit: A current curriculum vitae; A brief statement outlining your areas of expertise and teaching interests; and Details of any previous university teaching experience and availability for Summer Term and/or Semester 1. The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time. Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/Security-Shift-Supervisor_JR105862": {
      "title": "Security Shift Supervisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team Campus Operations & Services provides the highest quality facility management services to support the teaching, research, and commercial activities for Murdoch University. It oversees maintenance and strategic asset management planning for the University for the short, medium, and longer term. Security Services primary functions include: The protection of all people within the University, including staff, students, contractors and visitors. The protection of property. The prevention and detection of crime. Acting as initial first responders to incidents and emergencies on campus.   Your New Role!   The position has shift supervisory responsibility to ensure the safety and wellbeing of the University community and protection of property and assets. Operating on Monday to Friday, from 12:00am to 8:00am, the role provides security control room coordination, including incident response and escalation, supervision of the on-duty security officers, implementation of security operating procedures and emergency management guidelines, and performs the role of Chief Warden. Your key responsibilities will include – Providing proactive leadership and supervision of the rostered on-duty Security Officers to ensure that both scheduled and unplanned security requirements are delivered in accordance with policy and procedure. Within a control room environment, efficiently coordinate the monitoring of security systems including CCTV and electronic access control, and timely responses to alarm activations, calls, breach of behaviour, incidents and suspicious activity. Manage the recording of events and log activity that occur on shift, including drafting incident reports for management review and investigation. Conduct detailed handovers at the beginning and end of each shift, including effective completion of assigned tasks from Security Management. Coordinate incident and emergency responses in line with the University Critical Incident Management Plan and Security Operating Procedures. Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Continuous | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) position attracts a remuneration of $74,000 – $82,000 (plus applicable night shift penalties) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)   What you’ll bring to the role: Completion of a Certificate II or III Security with a current and valid Security License or equivalent competency. Substantial relevant security experience in a large and complex organisation, as well as coordinating emergency response services. Ability to effectively supervise and instruct staff and contractor employees. Demonstrated ability to lead by example and work productively as part of a team. Proficiency with Microsoft Office suite of products and security systems. Highly developed written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to liaise with people at all levels and backgrounds. Current “C” Class Driver’s License. The suitable applicant will be required to complete a fitness assessment and maintain an appropriate level of fitness for the physical standards and efficient performance required of this position. Please note, the successful candidate will be required to undertake a criminal record check in accordance with the University's Criminal Record Screening Procedure and Employee Background Checks Procedure.   Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Kay Rockley, Manager Security Services and quote JR105862 as the reference.   Applications Close on 08/11/2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    },
    "https://murdoch.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/MurdochCareers/job/Perth-WA/WIL-Coordinator_JR105520": {
      "title": "WIL Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nAbout The Team The Deputy Vice Chancellor (Education) portfolio leads Murdoch University’s commitment to delivering contemporary, accessible and inclusive education that support every student to succeed and graduate ready for their future careers. Within this portfolio, the Office of Learning, Teaching and Technology plays a central role in supporting high-quality teaching and learning experiences across the University. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) plays a vital role in this mission by providing students with practical, real-world experiences that enhance employability and career readiness. Working in partnership with Schools and industry stakeholders, the WIL team coordinates and supports student placements across a range of disciplines, delivering consistent, compliant and high-quality placement services and student experiences within a dynamic and complex environment. Your New Role!   As WIL Coordinator, you will play a key role in connecting students with meaningful, real-world placement experiences across a range of disciplines, including nursing, allied health and psychology. Working closely with the WIL Manager, you will lead and support your team in the effective delivery of WIL activities, building strong relationships with academic teams and industry partners, and helping to ensure a positive and consistent placement experience for all stakeholders across the placement cycle. Your key responsibilities include: Leading operational delivery of WIL placement activities, coordinating placement sourcing, matching, eligibility, readiness and documentation to ensure efficient, timely and high-quality placement experiences. Coordinating team operations and priorities , supporting placement cycles, allocating workloads, monitoring progress and ensuring deadlines and service standards are met. Building effective stakeholder relationships by providing responsive, high-quality service and working collaboratively with students, academic staff, placement supervisors, host organisations and university stakeholders. Driving continuous improvement by identifying opportunities to streamline processes, strengthen workflows, implement operational changes and promote consistent practices across the WIL Team. Ensuring quality, compliance and risk management by aligning operational practices with University policies, procedures and legislative requirements, supporting quality assurance and reporting, and managing complex issues and risks, including escalation as required.   Please refer to the Position Description for further details.   What We Offer You! This Continuous | Full Time (37.5 hours per week) attracts a remuneration of $93k – $112k (pro rata) plus 17% employer superannuation contributions.      You’ll join a dynamic and talented team where diversity and innovation thrive. Our Silver-tier status in the Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI), awarded in 2025, reflects our commitment to LGBTIQA+ inclusion, equity, and creating a safe, welcoming environment for all. We strive to be the university of choice for First Nations peoples, honouring Indigenous knowledge. Sustainability is central to our community and guided by clear, confident leadership, we are working toward an ambitious future with goals of net zero emissions and zero waste by 2030.   As well as the flexibility to maintain a work life balance, our staff enjoy a vibrant, natural campus with world-class facilities, along with a variety of benefits, including:   Flexible work arrangements Cultural Load and allowance - providing up to $8,944 per year to First Nations employees who are contributing cultural knowledge and perspectives beyond the scope of their role Indigenous Language Allowance Salary packaging options – such as purchasing leave, gym membership, car parking permit Employee Assistance Program On-campus services and facilities, such as a Childcare Centre, Gym, Vet Hospital, and Chiropractic Clinic   For further information, check out our benefits and services page !   Join us!   Please apply online via the Apply Now button, along with submitting the following documents to support your application - A cover letter including a statement addressing the selection criteria (with reference to the Position Description) Your most recent resume (CV)     What you’ll bring to the role: A relevant qualification and experience in higher education, student services, stakeholder-focused engagement, or related role. Proven leadership experience with the ability to motivate, develop and support high-performing teams while fostering a positive workplace culture. Demonstrated experience coordinating placement programs or WIL activities, with excellent organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities. Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to build and maintain effective partnerships across internal and external networks. Experience interpreting policies, procedures or compliance requirements and applying them accurately in practice High-level digital literacy and problem-solving capability, with experience using Microsoft Office and business systems, and the ability to adapt quickly to new technologies and processes   Previous experience in a health-related discipline would be an advantage, though not essential.   Applicants should refer to the Position Description for further details on the work requirements, duties, skills and experience required for this role. Applications sent by post or email will not be accepted. Please note visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants are expected to have current and valid work rights in Australia. Please see the  Applicant Guide  for more information. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process.   Contact Us   For enquiries about the opportunity on offer please reach out to Amanda Peterson, Work Integrated Learning Placement Manager, amanda.peterson@murdoch.edu.au and quote JR105520 as the reference.     Applications Close on 18/11/2026 (11:59pm AWST)   The University reserves the right to withdraw this advertisement at any time.     Murdoch University acknowledges the different perspectives, skills and experience that people from different backgrounds bring to strengthen its workforce. Murdoch University is committed to enhancing diversity in all its forms and strongly encourages suitably qualified candidates from Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples, women, people with disability, people of CaLD background and people of diverse genders to apply for this important position. Murdoch University values workplace diversity, promotes inclusion, and strongly encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders, women, and individuals with disability. Applicants who have support or access requirements, are encouraged to advise this at the time of their application, to ensure appropriate assistance is provided throughout the recruitment process."
    }
